two things they established that the landing had not. (a) there are FOUR polarity-sensitive
rewrites, not the two the commit message names -- 'on && !s_arHave' and the deleted bounds
check are the others -- and all four drop a constant-TRUE conjunct from a refusal, so the
rewrites preserve the expressions' VALUES rather than merely being unreachable. (b) binding 41
is never a null descriptor: set_claim opens 'if (!v2) v2 = s_dumView;', so the unconditional
VK_NULL_HANDLE resolves to the 1x1 dummy and no null-descriptor or robustness feature is
relied on.
all 14 findings were comment or documentation and every one was verified against the source
before acting. the two worth naming: A-F4, the comment this landing rewrote claims 'mirror is
the only allocation left in a TAGPU_GAFATLAS' and rlist is a second -- safe only because
free_buffers' one caller is the GUI atlas, whose rlist is always NULL, and atlas_setup memsets
afterwards, so it becomes a real leak the day the UI is given a list. NOT fixed here on
purpose: rlist's lifetime is 11-5e-2c's declared subject and a half-fix (free the buffer,
leave rlistWant/rlistFailed latched) is the shape this gate keeps finding, so the obligation
is written into 11-5e-2c's entry and the function's own comment. B-F2a, thirteen lines
documenting the deleted rgb_mirror_zeroed stayed behind and now read as documentation for
job_clear_dest, describing a hazard from a function that no longer exists.
B-F3 did NOT reproduce and chasing it found the real gap: it predicted one lost log line, the
line appeared zero times on main's own runs, and the reason was that the four-run A/B had
tagpu_gui.on OFF -- so the measurement labelled 'part 2 measured' had never entered the GUI
lane, which is the landing's subject. a second interleaved four with gui.on=1 covers it: all
twelve grabs one hash with the minimap cluster and the cursor's pixel at (512,384) masked, and
the finding then CONFIRMED at 1 line per main run and 0 per branch run. 'nothing observable
changes' is overstated by exactly that line, and the docs now say so.
fixes are in 03e92f3 and fda8451 and are comment-only -- proven by masking: every touched .c
and .h is byte-identical line-for-line to the reviewed tree -- so the measured binary is the
landed binary and no re-review.
